#14 4.599 brackets; typing carriage return will give you the default.
#14 4.599 
#14 4.599 On some of the questions which ask for file or directory names you are allowed
#14 4.599 to use the ~name construct to specify the login directory belonging to "name",
#14 4.599 even if you don't have a shell which knows about that.  Questions where this is
#14 4.599 allowed will be marked "(~name ok)".
#14 4.599 
#14 4.599 [Type carriage return to continue]  
#14 4.602 
#14 4.602 The prompter used in this script allows you to use shell variables and
#14 4.602 backticks in your answers.  You may use $1, $2, etc...  to refer to the words
#14 4.602 in the default answer, as if the default line was a set of arguments given to a
#14 4.602 script shell.  This means you may also use $* to repeat the whole default line,
#14 4.602 so you do not have to re-type everything to add something to the default.
#14 4.602 
#14 4.602 Every time there is a substitution, you will have to confirm.  If there is an
#14 4.602 error (e.g. an unmatched backtick), the default answer will remain unchanged
#14 4.602 and you will be prompted again.
#14 4.602 
#14 4.602 If you are in a hurry, you may run 'Configure -d'.  This will bypass nearly all
#14 4.602 the questions and use the computed defaults (or the previous answers if there
